# A game leaderboard. Build it, then give it a file name and it remembers between runs:
#   ./intent build examples/leaderboard.intent -o build/leaderboard
#   ./build/leaderboard scores.log

Players is a collection.
Each player has a name, a score (number) and a level (number).
No two players share the same name.
If a player already exists, replace it.

"ahead of" means score over.
"beginner" means with a level under 5.
A champion is a player whose score is at least 1000.

join: add a player.
Look up a player by name.
kick: remove a player by name.

award: increase the score by a given amount for the player whose name is a given name.
level-up: add 1 to the level of players whose name is a given name.
bonus: increase every score by 10 percent.

podium: show the top 3 players by score.
leader: show the name of the player with the highest score.
champions: show the names of the champions.
rivals: show the names of players ahead of a given score.
newcomers: show the beginner players sorted by name.

How many players are there?
What is the average score?
new-season: set the score to 0.
